From b39fb1dbb0ecce7a7e0bf52b05b4cabfbf52190a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:57:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/timer: TC waveform outputs on pins and capture (U2249)

The TC now drives the pads muxed to WO[1:0], as a PIC32CM MC00 does
(firmware/hello APP=tcprobe2): NFRQ and MFRQ toggle on CCx matches,
NPWM and MPWM set at the start and the wrap and clear on the match
counting up (the reverse counting down), the match winning on a shared
tick; INVENx inverts; a stopped TC drives low, a disabled one floats.
While a pad selects an output the counter steps through its changes.

Capture from the event input: OFF/RETRIGGER/COUNT/START and STAMP
capture COUNT on the active edge (TCINV), STAMP captures MAX at each
overflow, PPW/PWP capture period and width and restart, PW captures
the width, stops, and waits for the first active edge after the
enable. Each channel is a two-deep FIFO with ERR; a read moves the
buffer up and MCx returns two GCLK_TC cycles later (tcprobe3/4). A
start with COUNT = CCx sets MCx, as silicon does. A COPEN channel does
not drive its pad; capture on pins is not modelled yet.

qtest: pads, STAMP FIFO and overflow capture, PPW, PW.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
